# Build trees. More than one is routine now that so much is optional —
# CLOCKWORK_SCHEDULER, CLOCKWORK_DEVICE, CLOCKWORK_LINK and the sanitiser and
# coverage builds each want their own — so the pattern earns its keep as much
# as the plain name does.
build/
build-*/
dist/

# Cargo. Unanchored, unlike the `rust/target/` this replaces: a rule containing
# a slash is pinned to the repo root, so that one covered the workspace here and
# would have missed a crate added anywhere else.
target/

node_modules/
*.o
*.o.d

test-results/
playwright-report/

# Archives. A zip of build metadata (the .git directories under build-*/_deps/)
# has been swept in by `git add -A` twice: 6cd8481 untracked one and it came
# back, because untracking without a rule only treats the symptom. Nothing here
# ships as a zip, so the blanket rule costs nothing.
*.zip

# Editor, tool and OS noise — none of it ours to carry, and all of it arrives
# uninvited in a tree other people will now clone.
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.log

# The NIF suite's own mix output (test/nif).
test/nif/_build/
test/nif/deps/
